WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.850 --> 00:00:03.680
In our rapidly developing
world, the demand

00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:07.310
for well-educated workers
has never been greater.

00:00:07.310 --> 00:00:10.910
Yet for many, education
remains out of reach.

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:15.440
Worldwide 250 million
children are out of school.

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:20.070
Even more are unable to
read, write, or count.

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:22.800
Every day a growing
displaced population

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:26.050
abandons their
education, and others

00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:28.730
struggle to find new
modes of education

00:00:28.730 --> 00:00:31.910
to balance work with learning.

00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:34.790
At the Massachusetts
Institute of Technology,

00:00:34.790 --> 00:00:36.770
we believe everyone
should have access

00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:39.620
to a quality education
and a better tomorrow.

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:45.440
To help make that a reality,
MIT and Community Jameel

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:48.920
are launching the Abdul
Latif Jameel World Education

00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:51.410
Laboratory or J-WEL.

00:00:51.410 --> 00:00:55.070
Our mission: to bring
together the best minds

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:59.120
to transform education
and learning worldwide,

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:02.930
from pre-kindergarten through
higher education to workforce

00:01:02.930 --> 00:01:04.550
training.

00:01:04.550 --> 00:01:08.360
MIT has been a pioneer in the
field of digital learning,

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:12.680
opening our doors to the world
through OpenCourseWare, MITx,

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:17.760
edX, and most recently, the
MicroMasters Credential.

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:22.320
Join us now, as MIT and J-WEL
explore education across

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:27.450
cultures, backgrounds, and ages,
and collaborate with educators,

00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:30.360
universities,
governments, nonprofits,

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:34.350
and industries to find new
solutions in every area

00:01:34.350 --> 00:01:38.010
of education - from research
on learning and curriculum

00:01:38.010 --> 00:01:42.540
development, to teacher
education and public policy.

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:46.350
Our goal: to confront the
most pressing problems facing

00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:51.090
education today and deliver
sustainable, scalable,

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:54.360
impactful solutions
to the world.

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:58.430
As we transform learning,
we transform lives.

00:01:58.430 --> 00:02:02.100
Together, let's
learn how, and do it.

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:03.900
